{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Let her not be, I pray, as one dead.</b> Aaron said to Moses: I cannot examine the affliction, because I am a close relative, and a priest who is a close relative is disqualified from examining the affliction, and there is no other priest in the world. Therefore, if you do not pray for her, she has no remedy but will remain in her leprosy and never be healed. And this is what he said, ״אשר בצאתו מרחם אמו״ — as one who comes forth from his mother's womb — for one who is born a leper from his mother's womb has no purification ever, and so our Rabbis of blessed memory stated. Therefore he said: you must in any event pray for her, so that our sister not be like a leper, who is considered as one dead coming forth from his mother's womb, who has no purification ever. Or Scripture may say: let not our sister now be like the stillbirth of one dead, for when it comes forth from its mother's womb half its flesh is consumed, and so is the flesh of the leper."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:31:54.317050266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}